[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
       [1mtpm2[22m(1) - To ease installation of tpm2-tools in initrd or embedded systems where size-optimization and limited resources are important,  it  is  conve‐
       nient  to  have  a  single  executable  that can dispatch the various TPM2 functionalities specified by the argument which is one of the available tool
       names.

       The options and arguments that follow are either the [1mcommon options [22mor those specific to the [1mtool name[22m.

       It is important to note that individual tools with prefix [1mtpm2_ [22mcan still be invoked, however, they are now soft-linked to this [1mtpm2  [22mexecutable.   And
       so unlike BusyBox, full functionality of the individual tools is available in the executable.  For example: [1mtpm2_getrandom 8 [22mcan alternatively be spec‐
       ified as [1mtpm2 getrandom 8[22m.

